{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>רֵאשִׁית, etc. וְאַחֲרִיתוֹ, etc.</b> Meaning: the first of the nations concerning whom Israel were commanded to destroy — they were not commanded at the outset except concerning Amalek, as it is written (Exodus 17:14) ״כְּתֹב זֹאת זִכָּרוֹן וְגוֹ׳ מָחֹה אֶמְחֶה אֶת זֵכֶר עֲמָלֵק״, and this was close to their departure from Egypt, and they would wage war against him and pursue him. Saul did to him what he did; in the days of Mordecai Israel did to him what they did. And he said <b>וְאַחֲרִיתוֹ</b>, etc. — meaning, he will not stand at the point of final destruction but <b>עֲדֵי אוֹבֵד</b> — meaning, until King Messiah destroys the nations; then will the end of Amalek be to be utterly cut off." "Or it may intend in this manner: <b>רֵאשִׁית גּוֹיִם</b> — meaning, ״רֵאשִׁית״ in the sense of preeminence and importance — Amalek is the foremost of all the nations, and he will stand at this level until he reaches the point of his destruction. And that is what he says <b>וְאַחֲרִיתוֹ</b> — meaning, even though he is רֵאשִׁית גּוֹיִם — <b>עֲדֵי אוֹבֵד</b>, and there is praise for Israel that they will reach him at his hand when he is at the height of his greatness. And likewise he said <b>וְצִים מִיַּד כִּתִּים</b>, etc. — <b>וְגַם הוּא עֲדֵי אֹבֵד</b>: he too will become a portion for Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:02.507129577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}